/* =====================================================================
   Heparin-Induced Thrombocytopenia (HIT) — QSP Mechanistic Map
   including autoimmune HIT (aHIT), spontaneous HIT syndrome and VITT
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE ORGANISING IDEA

     HIT IS NOT A DRUG TOXICITY. IT IS AN IMMUNE COMPLEX DISEASE IN
     WHICH THE DRUG IS ONE HALF OF THE ANTIGEN.

   Every other adverse drug reaction in this library scales with drug
   exposure: more drug, more effect. HIT does not, and the reason is
   the single most important quantitative fact on this map:

     THE ANTIGEN IS A STOICHIOMETRIC COMPLEX, SO ITS ABUNDANCE IS A
     BELL-SHAPED FUNCTION OF HEPARIN CONCENTRATION, NOT A MONOTONIC ONE.

   Platelet factor 4 (PF4, CXCL4) is a 7.8 kDa homotetramer carrying a
   ring of lysines with a net charge near +20 at physiological pH.
   Heparin is a polyanion. When the two meet at roughly charge-neutral
   molar ratio they do not merely bind — they polymerise into
   ULTRALARGE COMPLEXES (ULCs, >670 kDa, ~50-100 nm) in which multiple
   PF4 tetramers are strung along and between heparin chains. Only the
   ULC is antigenic, because only the ULC presents the neoepitope at
   the surface density needed for multivalent IgG binding, and only
   multivalent IgG can crosslink FcγRIIa.

   Two consequences follow, and both are clinical facts:

     1. ADD MORE HEPARIN AND THE ANTIGEN DISAPPEARS. In excess heparin
        each PF4 tetramer is coated by its own chain, the polymer
        cannot bridge, ULCs dissolve. This is not a curiosity — it is
        the confirmatory step of the serotonin release assay (SRA):
        platelet activation at 0.1-0.3 U/mL heparin that is ABOLISHED
        at 100 U/mL is what makes the test diagnostic. A model whose
        antigen curve is monotonic in heparin cannot reproduce the very
        assay used to diagnose the disease.

     2. THE POLYMER NEEDS LENGTH. Bridging requires a chain long enough
        to reach two PF4 tetramers: roughly ≥ 11-14 saccharide units.
        Unfractionated heparin (mean ~15 kDa, ~50 saccharides) bridges
        superbly; low-molecular-weight heparin (~4.5 kDa) bridges
        poorly; fondaparinux (a 5-saccharide synthetic pentasaccharide)
        essentially cannot. The clinical risk ordering — UFH ≫ LMWH ≫
        fondaparinux, roughly 10x per step — is therefore a PROPERTY OF
        CHAIN LENGTH and is drawn here as such rather than asserted.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE THREE LAYERS IN SERIES, AND THE ONE LOOP THAT CLOSES ON ITSELF

     LAYER 1  ANTIGEN     PF4 + heparin → ULC.  Bell-shaped in heparin,
              (clusters 1-4)  gated by chain length, saturable in PF4.
                              Cut by: STOPPING HEPARIN (and by nothing
                              else, which is why cessation is step one).

     LAYER 2  IMMUNITY    ULC → marginal-zone B cell / complement-
              (clusters 5-8)  assisted BCR engagement → anti-PF4/heparin
                              IgG. Peculiar kinetics: detectable at day
                              4-5 even on FIRST exposure (pre-existing
                              clones, no classical IgM→IgG switch),
                              and TRANSIENT — median seroreversion ~50 d
                              (functional) to ~85-100 d (immunoassay) —
                              with NO ANAMNESTIC BOOST on re-exposure.
                              Cut by: plasma exchange, rituximab, time.

     LAYER 3  EFFECTOR    IgG·ULC → FcγRIIa clustering on platelets and
              (clusters 9-16) monocytes → ITAM/Syk/PLCγ2 → activation →
                              (a) platelet consumption   → THROMBOCYTOPENIA
                              (b) PF4 α-granule release  → BACK TO LAYER 1
                              (c) PS+ microparticles + monocyte tissue
                                  factor + NETs → THROMBIN BURST → THROMBOSIS
                              Cut by: IVIG (receptor competition), and
                              downstream only by anticoagulants.

     THE LOOP is (b). Activated platelets dump PF4 — the very antigen
     precursor — into the plasma they are being activated in. Antigen
     makes activation makes antigen. This autocatalytic arm is drawn in
     bold red, and it is why HIT is explosive rather than graded, why
     platelet counts fall over hours once they start falling, and why
     PLATELET TRANSFUSION IS ANTI-THERAPY: it feeds the loop its
     substrate. It is also why stopping heparin alone leaves the loop
     partially fuelled and a ~50% residual 30-day thrombosis risk.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE CENTRAL PARADOX THE MAP MUST EXPLAIN

     A DISEASE DEFINED BY A LOW PLATELET COUNT WHOSE PATIENTS DIE OF CLOTS.

   Two outputs, one driver. The same FcγRIIa signal that marks platelets
   for splenic clearance (→ nadir, typically 40-80 x10⁹/L, a FALL of
   >50% mattering far more than any absolute value) simultaneously sheds
   phosphatidylserine-exposing microparticles and drives monocyte tissue
   factor. Thrombin generation in HIT is among the highest measured in
   any acquired thrombophilia. Bleeding is rare; thrombosis occurs in
   20-50% of untreated patients. Therefore the map deliberately routes
   PLT_ACT to BOTH sinks, and the model computes both, so that any
   intervention can be scored on the two axes independently — which is
   exactly how the drug classes separate:

     STOP HEPARIN     cuts antigen        → both axes, slowly
     ARGATROBAN/      cuts thrombin only  → thrombosis axis only;
       BIVALIRUDIN                          platelets recover on their own
                                            schedule, not the drug's
     IVIG             cuts effector       → both axes, within 24-48 h
     PLATELET TXN     feeds the loop      → worsens the thrombosis axis
                                            while cosmetically fixing the
                                            platelet axis
     WARFARIN EARLY   cuts protein C
                        FASTER than
                        prothrombin       → transiently WORSENS thrombosis

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE TWO PHARMACOLOGICAL TRAPS, DRAWN AS MECHANISM

   (i) THE WARFARIN / VENOUS LIMB GANGRENE TRAP  (cluster 19)
       Protein C has a plasma half-life of ~8 h; prothrombin (FII) ~60-72 h.
       Start a vitamin K antagonist while thrombin generation is still
       maximal and the anticoagulant limb collapses within a day while
       the procoagulant limb is still nearly intact. Net thrombin
       generation RISES. In a limb already thrombosed with an intact
       arterial supply the result is venous limb gangrene — amputation
       in a patient who was "being anticoagulated". This is why guidance
       is to withhold VKA until platelets recover above ~150 x10⁹/L and
       to overlap ≥5 days. The half-life mismatch is on the map because
       the model must GENERATE the trap, not warn about it.

   (ii) THE ARGATROBAN-INR TRAP  (cluster 19)
       Argatroban, a direct thrombin inhibitor, prolongs the PT/INR
       substantially without any vitamin-K-dependent factor depletion.
       An INR of 4 on argatroban + warfarin does not mean the warfarin
       is therapeutic; factor X activity may still be near normal.
       Stop the argatroban on that INR and the patient is uncovered.
       The map carries INR as a MEASUREMENT node fed by two distinct
       inputs (true factor depletion, and DTI assay artifact) so the
       dissociation is explicit.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE ICEBERG, AND WHY THRESHOLDS ARE DRAWN EXPLICITLY

   After cardiac surgery with cardiopulmonary bypass, ~25-50% of patients
   seroconvert on PF4 immunoassay, ~2-5% have a platelet-activating
   antibody by SRA, and ~1-3% develop clinical HIT. The antibody is
   common; the disease is not. The map therefore separates:

       ANTIBODY PRESENT  →  PLATELET-ACTIVATING (functional)  →  CLINICAL

   as three successive thresholds — epitope specificity and affinity,
   then achieved FcγRIIa crosslinking density, then crossing of the
   platelet-count and thrombosis endpoints. Cluster 20 renders these as
   the assays that measure each level (ELISA optical density, SRA %
   release, HIPA), so the model can output an OD and an SRA rather than
   a hidden internal state.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE VARIANTS AS ONE PARAMETER, NOT ONE MORE MODEL  (cluster 22)

   Autoimmune HIT, spontaneous HIT syndrome and VITT share this entire
   map with a single change: their antibodies bind PF4 at or near the
   HEPARIN-BINDING SITE itself and can cluster PF4 WITHOUT heparin.
   Formally that is a heparin-independence coefficient moving from 0
   toward 1. Everything clinically strange about them then follows:
   the platelet count keeps falling after heparin is stopped (there is
   nothing left to stop), the disease is more severe and more often
   arterial or cerebral-venous, high-dose IVIG works because receptor
   competition does not care where the antibody bound, and — critically —
   heparin is NOT contraindicated in VITT because there is no heparin in
   the antigen. Drawing this as one coefficient rather than one more
   subgraph is the point: it is the same disease seen through a
   different epitope.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Legend
     ellipse              biological species / state
     box                  process, flux or compartment
     hexagon              drug or intervention
     octagon              clinical endpoint
     diamond              laboratory measurement / assay
     doubleoctagon        iatrogenic harm / adverse outcome
     solid arrow          activation / increase
     T-bar (tee)          inhibition / decrease
     dashed               slow, transcriptional or delayed change
     bold red             the PF4 autocatalytic amplification loop
     blue                 pharmacological intervention
     orange               iatrogenic harm
   ===================================================================== */

digraph HIT_QSP {
  graph [rankdir=TB, newrank=true, splines=spline, overlap=false, nodesep=0.22,
         ranksep=0.60, fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=11,
         labelloc="t", compound=true, bgcolor="white",
         label=<<b>Heparin-Induced Thrombocytopenia (HIT) — Immune Complex Thrombosis</b><br/>
                <font point-size="12">QSP mechanistic map · antigen stoichiometry → transient immunity → FcγRIIa effector · PF4 autocatalytic loop · aHIT / VITT as one coefficient</font>>];
  node  [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9, style="filled", penwidth=0.9];
  edge  [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=8, arrowsize=0.6, penwidth=0.9, color="#555555"];

  /* ================================================================
     1. HEPARIN EXPOSURE AND PHARMACOKINETICS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_hep {
    label="1 · 헤파린 노출과 약동학 (Heparin Exposure & PK)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#5C6BC0"; fillcolor="#E8EAF6"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, fillcolor="#C5CAE9", color="#5C6BC0"];

    HEP_IND   [label="적응증 / 노출 상황\nIndication for heparin\n(VTE Tx/Px, ACS, CPB,\nHD circuit, line flush)"];
    HEP_UFH   [label="미분획 헤파린 (UFH)\nUnfractionated heparin\nmean ~15 kDa, ~45-50 saccharides\npolydisperse 5-30 kDa"];
    HEP_LMWH  [label="저분자량 헤파린 (LMWH)\nEnoxaparin ~4.5 kDa\n(~15 saccharides)\ndalteparin ~6 kDa"];
    HEP_FONDA [label="폰다파리눅스\nFondaparinux\nsynthetic PENTAsaccharide\n1728 Da — 5 units only"];
    HEP_DANA  [label="다나파로이드\nDanaparoid\nheparan/dermatan/chondroitin\nsulfate mixture"];
    HEP_DOSE  [label="총 노출량 및 기간\nCumulative dose × duration\n(therapeutic ≫ prophylactic\n≫ flush-only)"];
    HEP_CPB   [label="심폐우회로 헤파린 볼루스\nCPB heparin bolus\n300-400 U/kg → plasma\n3-6 U/mL (very high)"];
    HEP_PK1   [label="UFH 혈장 농도\n[UFH] plasma\nsaturable RES clearance +\nlinear renal (t½ 30-90 min,\ndose-dependent)"];
    HEP_PK2   [label="LMWH 혈장 항Xa\n[LMWH] anti-Xa\nSC F≈0.9, t½ 4-6 h,\nrenal CL"];
    HEP_PK3   [label="폰다 혈장 농도\n[Fondaparinux]\nSC F≈1.0, t½ 17-21 h,\npurely renal"];
    HEP_CHAIN [label="사슬 길이 분포\nCHAIN LENGTH distribution\nbridging requires ≥11-14\nsaccharides (>5.4 kDa)"];
    HEP_STOP  [label="헤파린 중단\nHEPARIN CESSATION\n— the only manoeuvre that\ncuts the ANTIGEN itself"];
    HEP_GAG   [label="내인성 GAG\nEndogenous polyanions\n(heparan sulfate, polyP,\nchondroitin sulfate, DNA/RNA,\nbacterial LPS)"];
    HEP_REEXP [label="재노출\nRe-exposure\n(timing vs seroreversion\ndetermines rapid-onset HIT)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     2. PF4 BIOLOGY — THE OTHER HALF OF THE ANTIGEN
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_pf4 {
    label="2 · PF4 생물학 (Platelet Factor 4 / CXCL4)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#EF6C00"; fillcolor="#FFF3E0"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#FFE0B2", color="#EF6C00"];

    PF4_GENE  [label="PF4 (CXCL4) 유전자\nmegakaryocyte-restricted\nexpression"];
    PF4_GRAN  [label="α-과립 PF4 저장고\nα-granule PF4 store\n~ 3 µg per 10⁹ platelets\n(most abundant platelet protein)"];
    PF4_TET   [label="PF4 사량체\nPF4 HOMOTETRAMER\n7.8 kDa, net charge ≈ +20\nlysine ring (K61,K62,K65,K66)"];
    PF4_PLAS  [label="혈장 유리 PF4\nFree plasma PF4\nbaseline 2-10 ng/mL →\n>100-1000 ng/mL when activated"];
    PF4_SURF  [label="혈소판 표면 결합 PF4\nSurface-bound PF4\non platelet CS-GAG"];
    PF4_EC    [label="내피 HSPG 결합 PF4\nPF4 on endothelial\nheparan sulfate\n(tissue reservoir, large)"];
    PF4_MONO  [label="단핵구 표면 PF4\nPF4 on monocyte GAG\n(CD14+ surface antigen —\nkey to TF induction)"];
    PF4_CONF  [label="PF4 구조 변화\nCONFORMATIONAL CHANGE\ncompact → open;\nβ-sheet rearrangement on\npolyanion binding"];
    PF4_NEO   [label="네오에피토프 노출\nNEOEPITOPE exposure\n(KKO-defined site;\nP34-L36 / site 1+2)"];
    PF4_KD    [label="PF4-heparin 친화도\nKd ≈ 10-100 nM\n(chain-length dependent)"];
    PF4_HBS   [label="헤파린 결합 부위\nHeparin-binding site\n(the VITT epitope —\nsee cluster 22)"];
    PF4_CLEAR [label="PF4 소실\nPF4 clearance\nt½ ~ 10-20 min free;\nhours when GAG-bound"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     3. ANTIGEN ASSEMBLY — THE BELL-SHAPED STOICHIOMETRY
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_ag {
    label="3 · 항원 조립 — 화학량론적 종 (Antigen Assembly · ULC Stoichiometry)  ★ 모델의 핵심 비선형성";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#C62828"; fillcolor="#FFEBEE"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, fillcolor="#FFCDD2", color="#C62828"];

    AG_RATIO  [label="PF4 : 헤파린 몰비\nPF4 : heparin MOLAR RATIO\noptimal ≈ 1 : 1 by charge\n(≈ 27-32 PF4 per UFH chain\nby mass)"];
    AG_NEUT   [label="전하 중성화\nCHARGE NEUTRALISATION\nnear-zero net charge is the\nrequirement for polymerisation"];
    AG_BIN    [label="이량체/소복합체\nSmall PF4·heparin complexes\n(1:1, non-antigenic —\ntoo few epitopes)"];
    AG_ULC    [label="초거대 복합체 (ULC)\nULTRALARGE COMPLEX\n>670 kDa, 50-100 nm\nMULTIPLE PF4 tetramers per\nheparin, MULTIPLE chains\n★ THE ANTIGEN"];
    AG_BELL   [label="종형 용량-반응\nBELL-SHAPED in [heparin]\npeak at optimal ratio;\nFALLS at heparin excess"];
    AG_EXCESS [label="헤파린 과잉 해리\nHEPARIN EXCESS dissociation\neach PF4 gets its own chain →\nno bridging → ULC dissolves\n(= SRA 100 U/mL confirm step)"];
    AG_PF4EX  [label="PF4 과잉\nPF4 excess\n(also suboptimal: chains\nsaturated, no free bridging\nsegments)"];
    AG_LEN    [label="사슬 길이 게이팅\nCHAIN-LENGTH GATING\nUFH ≫ LMWH ≫ fonda\n≈ 10x risk per step"];
    AG_EPDENS [label="에피토프 표면 밀도\nEpitope surface DENSITY\n— sets IgG multivalency,\nnot merely total antigen"];
    AG_STAB   [label="복합체 안정성\nULC stability / t½\nstabilised once IgG-bound\n(antibody as crosslinker)"];
    AG_LOCAL  [label="국소 고농도 미세환경\nLocal microenvironment\n(platelet surface, injured\nendothelium: [PF4] ≫ plasma)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     4. NEOEPITOPE AND ANTIGEN PRESENTATION
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_neo {
    label="4 · 네오에피토프와 항원 제시 (Neoepitope & Antigen Handling)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#AD1457"; fillcolor="#FCE4EC"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#F8BBD0", color="#AD1457"];

    NEO_CRYPT [label="은닉 에피토프 노출\nCryptic epitope exposure\n(only in ULC-bound PF4)"];
    NEO_KKO   [label="KKO 모방 에피토프\nKKO-defined pathogenic epitope\n(murine monoclonal surrogate\nof human pathogenic IgG)"];
    NEO_RTO   [label="RTO 비병원성 에피토프\nRTO-defined monomeric epitope\n(binds PF4 monomer —\nNON-pathogenic; explains\nnon-activating antibodies)"];
    NEO_C3    [label="복합체 표면 C3 침착\nC3b/iC3b deposition on ULC\n(classical pathway,\nantibody-independent priming)"];
    NEO_CR2   [label="B세포 CR2(CD21) 보조자극\nCR2/CD21 co-engagement\nlowers BCR activation threshold"];
    NEO_APC   [label="항원 제시 세포\nAntigen-presenting cell\n(splenic MZ macrophage, DC)"];
    NEO_TDEP  [label="T세포 의존성 (부분적)\nPartial T-cell dependence\nCD4+ help; but response is\nfast and IgM-switch-independent"];
    NEO_PRE   [label="사전 존재 클론\nPRE-EXISTING B-cell clones\n(anti-PF4 reactivity in ~4-6%\nof healthy donors — explains\nday-4 IgG on FIRST exposure)"];
    NEO_MZB   [label="변연부 B세포\nMarginal-zone B cell\n(spleen; T-independent-like\nrapid IgG response)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     5. B-CELL ACTIVATION AND ANTIBODY PRODUCTION
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_bcell {
    label="5 · B세포 활성화와 항체 생성 (B-cell Activation & Antibody Production)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#6A1B9A"; fillcolor="#F3E5F5"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, fillcolor="#E1BEE7", color="#6A1B9A"];

    B_NAIVE   [label="미성숙/기억 B세포 풀\nNaive + pre-existing\nanti-PF4 B-cell pool"];
    B_ACT     [label="B세포 활성화\nB-cell activation\n(BCR + CR2 + TLR9/polyanion\nco-signal)"];
    B_PROLIF  [label="클론 증식\nClonal proliferation\n(doubling ~12-24 h)"];
    B_PLASMA  [label="단기 형질세포\nSHORT-LIVED plasmablast\nt½ ~ 3-5 days\n★ dominant source"];
    B_LLPC    [label="장기 형질세포\nLong-lived plasma cell\nMINIMAL in HIT\n★ absence explains transience\nAND absence of memory boost"];
    B_MEM     [label="기억 B세포\nMemory B cell\nfunctionally deficient →\nNO ANAMNESTIC RESPONSE\non re-exposure"];
    B_CD20    [label="CD20 발현\nCD20 on B cells\n(rituximab target — spares\nplasma cells)"];
    B_BAFF    [label="BAFF / APRIL 생존 신호\nplasmablast survival"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     6. ANTI-PF4/HEPARIN ANTIBODY REPERTOIRE
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_ab {
    label="6 · 항 PF4/헤파린 항체 레퍼토리 (Anti-PF4/Heparin Antibody Repertoire)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#283593"; fillcolor="#E8EAF6"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#C5CAE9", color="#283593"];

    AB_IGG    [label="항 PF4/H IgG\nAnti-PF4/heparin IgG\n★ the pathogenic isotype\n(IgG1/IgG3 dominant)"];
    AB_IGM    [label="항 PF4/H IgM\nnon-pathogenic\n(cannot engage FcγRIIa)"];
    AB_IGA    [label="항 PF4/H IgA\nnon-pathogenic"];
    AB_PATH   [label="병원성 하위분획\nPLATELET-ACTIVATING subset\n(the functional antibody —\na MINORITY of all IgG:\nthe iceberg's waterline)"];
    AB_NONP   [label="비활성화 IgG\nNon-activating IgG\n(low affinity, RTO-like,\nor wrong epitope) —\nseropositive, disease-free"];
    AB_TITRE  [label="항체 역가\nIgG titre / concentration"];
    AB_AFF    [label="친화도 및 결합가\nAffinity + VALENCY\n(bivalent IgG on high-density\nepitope = high avidity)"];
    AB_STOICH [label="면역복합체 (IgG·ULC)\nIMMUNE COMPLEX IgG·PF4·heparin\n★ the effector species"];
    AB_HDEP   [label="헤파린 의존성 계수\nHEPARIN-DEPENDENCE coefficient\nclassic HIT ≈ 1 → aHIT/VITT ≈ 0\n★ ONE parameter = ALL variants"];
    AB_CLEAR  [label="IgG 소실\nIgG catabolism\nFcRn-protected, t½ ~21 d;\nfunctional seroreversion ~50 d,\nimmunoassay ~85-100 d"];
    AB_CROSS  [label="교차반응성\nCross-reactivity\nLMWH ~ 90%, danaparoid ~10-25%,\nfondaparinux ~0-5%"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     7. ANTIBODY KINETICS AND THE TIMING OF HIT
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_kin {
    label="7 · 항체 동역학과 HIT 발병 시점 (Antibody Kinetics & Timing)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#00695C"; fillcolor="#E0F2F1"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, fillcolor="#B2DFDB", color="#00695C"];

    K_TYPICAL [label="전형적 HIT\nTYPICAL-onset HIT\nplatelet fall DAY 5-10\n(median day 6)\n★ delay is the immune\nmaturation time"];
    K_RAPID   [label="급속 발병 HIT\nRAPID-onset HIT\n<24 h — requires PRE-FORMED\nantibody from exposure within\nthe last ~100 days"];
    K_DELAY   [label="지연 발병 HIT\nDELAYED-onset HIT\nstarts or worsens AFTER heparin\nstopped (days-weeks) —\nheparin-independent antibody"];
    K_PERSIST [label="항체 지속 기간\nAntibody persistence window\n★ determines whether re-exposure\ngives rapid-onset HIT or nothing"];
    K_NOBOOST [label="기억 반응 결여\nNO anamnestic boost\nre-exposure at >100 d behaves\nlike a FIRST exposure\n★ a NEGATIVE prediction"];
    K_SEROREV [label="혈청 역전\nSeroreversion\nfunctional assay first,\nimmunoassay later"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     8. FcγRIIa ENGAGEMENT AND SIGNALLING
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_fcr {
    label="8 · FcγRIIa 결합과 신호전달 (FcγRIIa Crosslinking & ITAM Signalling)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#00838F"; fillcolor="#E0F7FA"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#B2EBF2", color="#00838F"];

    FCR_NUM   [label="혈소판 FcγRIIa 수\nFcγRIIa (CD32a) copies\n~1000-4000 per platelet"];
    FCR_POLY  [label="FcγRIIa 131 H/R 다형성\nH131 vs R131\n(binding affinity for IgG2/IgG1;\nmodifies HIT risk & severity)"];
    FCR_BOUND [label="점유된 FcγRIIa\nOccupied FcγRIIa"];
    FCR_XLINK [label="수용체 가교결합\nRECEPTOR CROSSLINKING\n★ MULTIVALENT complexes only —\nmonovalent binding does nothing"];
    FCR_THR   [label="가교 밀도 임계값\nCrosslinking-density THRESHOLD\n★ the second waterline of\nthe iceberg"];
    FCR_ITAM  [label="ITAM 인산화\nITAM phosphorylation"];
    FCR_SYK   [label="Syk 키나아제\nSyk activation"];
    FCR_LAT   [label="LAT / SLP-76 어댑터"];
    FCR_PLC   [label="PLCγ2 → IP₃ + DAG"];
